// @id 01M7J3NX5A4G0YNJA4A42NVQNV model=cloze
q: ==Friction== is the force resisting the relative motion of solid surfaces, fluid layers, and material elements sliding or grinding against each other.

// @id 01M7J3NX5A3H3DGREF5884GJ3W model=cloze
q: ==Dry== friction resists relative lateral motion of two solid surfaces in contact.

// @id 01M7J3NX5ABKWE12MB2DM82HM8 model=basic-example
q: The two regimes of dry friction are.. 
a: - **static friction** ("stiction") between non-moving surfaces
- **kinetic friction** (sometimes called sliding friction or dynamic friction) between moving surfaces
